<title>JAPAN: Big Japan aluminium mills' Dec output up 5.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Big Japan aluminium mills' Dec output up 5.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output of milled aluminium products at Japan's seven large fabricators rose 5.8 percent in December from the same month a year earlier to 119,446 tonnes, according to data submitted by the companies to the Japan Aluminum Federation and released on Monday.</p>
<p>The November data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Dec 96	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	    119,446	  +5.8 pct</p>
<p> Flat-rolled     92,086	  +4.2 pct</p>
<p>   Can stock     27,920	  -3.0 pct</p>
<p> Extrusions	27,360	 +11.5 pct</p>
<p>The seven companies are: Kobe Steel Ltd (includes KAAL joint venture with Alcoa), Sumitomo Light Metal Industries Ltd, Furukawa Electric Co, Mitsubishi Aluminum Co, Nippon Light Metal Co, Sky Aluminium Co and Showa Aluminum Corp.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
